---
import Base from '../../layouts/Base.astro';
import NextProject from '../../components/NextProject.astro';
---
<Base title="EventGem · Tejitha Kristem" description="EventGem case study: a live ticketing platform for Indian festivals and concerts overseas." calm>
  <article style="--accent: var(--marigold)">
    <header class="cs-head">
      <div class="wrap">
        <a class="back" href="/projects"><span class="arr">←</span> All projects</a>
        <span class="eyebrow mono">Hero project · Event ticketing platform</span>
        <h1 class="cs-title">Event<span class="accent">Gem</span></h1>
        <p class="cs-sub">The festive-season bestie for Indians overseas. <span class="hl">Every celebration, one roof.</span></p>
        <ul class="chips">
          <li class="live">● Live product</li>
          <li>Web + mobile + scanner</li>
          <li>UX/UI designer</li>
        </ul>
        <dl class="tldr">
          <div><dt class="mono">What it is</dt><dd>Ticketing for Indian festivals and concerts abroad</dd></div>
          <div><dt class="mono">Who it's for</dt><dd>Organizers, attendees and door managers</dd></div>
          <div><dt class="mono">My role</dt><dd>UX/UI designer, first brief to launch</dd></div>
          <div><dt class="mono">Team</dt><dd>Senior designers, a developer, testers, a content writer and two founders</dd></div>
        </dl>
        <div class="cs-hero-img rise"><img src="/images/eventgem-hero.webp" alt="EventGem organizer dashboard, event discovery and live scan screens on three phones" width="1441" height="900" /></div>
      </div>
    </header>

    <section class="cs-sec">
      <div class="wrap">
        <span class="step mono">01 · The gap</span>
        <h2 class="reveal">Indian events abroad were <em>lost in the noise</em></h2>
        <div class="prose">
          <p>Indian communities overseas had no single place to find and book their own events: community gatherings, festivals, Indian concerts. Organizers had no simple way to sell tickets, see how sales were going, or check people in at the door.</p>
        </div>
        <div class="boxes">
          <div class="box rise"><span class="k mono">Cluttered</span><h3>Events get buried</h3><p>On other platforms they sit next to real estate, cars and classes.</p></div>
          <div class="box rise"><span class="k mono">Pricey</span><h3>Fees on fees</h3><p>Attendees and organizers both pay heavily, even for small gatherings.</p></div>
          <div class="box rise"><span class="k mono">One-size</span><h3>No role gets its own flow</h3><p>Organizers, attendees and door managers all share one generic experience.</p></div>
        </div>
      </div>
    </section>

    <section class="cs-sec">
      <div class="wrap">
        <span class="step mono">02 · The idea</span>
        <h2 class="reveal">Every Indian celebration abroad, <em>under one roof</em></h2>
        <div class="boxes" style="--cols: 2">
          <div class="box rise">
            <span class="k mono">Small</span>
            <h3>Community events around you</h3>
            <div class="tags"><span>Garba</span><span>Holi</span><span>Dandiya</span><span>Diwali</span></div>
            <p>Around 30 guests, run by local organizers.</p>
          </div>
          <div class="box rise">
            <span class="k mono">Big</span>
            <h3>Live concerts</h3>
            <div class="tags"><span>Indian singers</span><span>Garba & dandiya nights</span></div>
            <p>500+ people dancing to live music.</p>
          </div>
        </div>
        <ul class="chain">
          <li>Only Indian events</li><li class="arrow" aria-hidden="true">✺</li><li>Low fees</li><li class="arrow" aria-hidden="true">✺</li><li class="end">Made for every role</li>
        </ul>
      </div>
    </section>

    <section class="cs-sec">
      <div class="wrap">
        <span class="step mono">03 · Process</span>
        <h2 class="reveal">How we got there</h2>
        <div class="prose"><p>Each step handed something to the next. Design and feedback kept looping, even after launch.</p></div>
        <div class="boxes" style="--cols: 4">
          <div class="box rise"><span class="k mono">Step 1</span><h3>Stakeholder interviews</h3><p>What the founders want, and how it should feel.</p></div>
          <div class="box rise"><span class="k mono">Step 2</span><h3>Competitor research</h3><p>Where existing platforms fall short.</p></div>
          <div class="box rise"><span class="k mono">Step 3</span><h3>Personas</h3><p>One for each role.</p></div>
          <div class="box rise"><span class="k mono">Step 4 ⇄ 5</span><h3>Design and feedback</h3><p>Flows, screens and the visual system, reviewed by the founders and real users.</p></div>
        </div>
      </div>
    </section>

    <section class="cs-sec">
      <div class="wrap">
        <span class="step mono">04 · Personas</span>
        <h2 class="reveal">Three people make these <em>events happen</em></h2>
        <div class="boxes">
          <div class="box rise">
            <span class="k mono">Organizer · mostly 45 to 60+</span>
            <blockquote>"I want to host a dandiya night for my community, and get paid without the hassle."</blockquote>
            <ul><li>Create events with different ticket types</li><li>Sell tickets and track sales</li><li>Choose who checks people in</li><li>Get paid after the event</li></ul>
          </div>
          <div class="box rise">
            <span class="k mono">Attendee · mostly 20 to 40</span>
            <blockquote>"I want to find Indian festivals and concerts near me, without digging through everything else."</blockquote>
            <ul><li>See every Indian event in one place</li><li>Get an event at a glance</li><li>Book on phone or laptop</li><li>Have the ticket ready at the door</li></ul>
          </div>
          <div class="box rise">
            <span class="k mono">Door manager · mostly under 40</span>
            <blockquote>"I need to get a crowd through the door quickly, even if I've never done this before."</blockquote>
            <ul><li>Start scanning on their own phone</li><li>A clear yes or no for every ticket</li><li>Keep the queue moving</li><li>Help when something goes wrong</li></ul>
          </div>
        </div>
      </div>
    </section>

    <section class="cs-sec">
      <div class="wrap">
        <span class="step mono">05 · Product</span>
        <h2 class="reveal">What each role gets</h2>

        <div class="role stack rise">
          <div class="role-head">
            <div><span class="k mono">Organizer</span><h3>One stop, from idea to payout</h3></div>
            <dl><div><dt>Create the event</dt><dd>Name, date, venue and details in one simple flow</dd></div><div><dt>Sell and track</dt><dd>Tickets, timed offers, cancellations and live sales analytics</dd></div><div><dt>Run the night</dt><dd>Assign door managers and watch live scanning data</dd></div><div><dt>After the event</dt><dd>Final results and payout from the platform</dd></div></dl>
          </div>
          <figure class="vid">
            <video src="/videos/eventgem-organizer.mp4" poster="/images/eventgem-organizer-poster.webp" width="1280" height="732" preload="none" muted loop playsinline controls data-autoplay aria-label="Organizer walkthrough video"></video>
          </figure>
        </div>

        <div class="role stack rise">
          <div class="role-head">
            <div><span class="k mono">Attendee</span><h3>Every Indian event nearby, zero noise</h3></div>
            <dl><div><dt>Only Indian events</dt><dd>Festivals, concerts and dances, nothing else</dd></div><div><dt>All in one place</dt><dd>Every festive gathering nearby, side by side</dd></div><div><dt>Desktop and mobile</dt><dd>Book wherever they are</dd></div><div><dt>Ticket in hand</dt><dd>A QR code ready for the door</dd></div></dl>
          </div>
          <figure class="vid">
            <video src="/videos/eventgem-attendee.mp4" poster="/images/eventgem-attendee-poster.webp" width="1280" height="732" preload="none" muted loop playsinline controls data-autoplay aria-label="Attendee walkthrough video: discover, event page, book, QR ticket"></video>
          </figure>
        </div>

        <div class="role stack rise">
          <div class="role-head">
            <div><span class="k mono">Door manager</span><h3>Just what they need, in the moment</h3></div>
            <dl><div><dt>No app to install</dt><dd>Open the organizer's link on their own phone</dd></div><div><dt>Ready in seconds</dt><dd>The organizer has already set up their account</dd></div><div><dt>Scan and go</dt><dd>A clear yes or no, then the next person</dd></div><div><dt>Backup when needed</dt><dd>The organizer can step in if anything goes wrong</dd></div></dl>
          </div>
          <figure class="vid">
            <video src="/videos/eventgem-door-manager.mp4" poster="/images/eventgem-door-manager-poster.webp" width="1280" height="732" preload="none" muted loop playsinline controls data-autoplay aria-label="Door manager walkthrough video"></video>
          </figure>
        </div>
      </div>
    </section>

    <section class="cs-sec">
      <div class="wrap">
        <span class="step mono">06 · Plot twists</span>
        <h2 class="reveal">Three times real life <em>edited the plan</em></h2>
        <div class="prose"><p>Two happened mid-build. One happened after launch. Each one made the product better.</p></div>

        <div class="moment rise">
          <div class="tagrow"><span class="num">#1</span><span class="status-chip">During the build</span></div>
          <h3>New name, new look, same deadline</h3>
          <div class="prose"><p>Around month seven the client asked for a new name, logo and design system: Eventful became EventGem. Requirements kept shifting with first-time founders, so I flagged the pattern and we moved to a documented requirements process. The rest of the build got way calmer.</p></div>
          <div class="palette">
            <div>
              <span class="lbl before mono">Before · Eventful</span>
              <div class="swatches"><i style="background:#024DDF">#024DDF</i><i class="lt" style="background:#FFFFFF">#FFFFFF</i><i style="background:#121212">#121212</i></div>
            </div>
            <div>
              <span class="lbl after mono">After · EventGem</span>
              <div class="swatches"><i style="background:#F98A45">#F98A45</i><i class="lt" style="background:#F9F4F0">#F9F4F0</i><i style="background:#344054">#344054</i><i style="background:#101828">#101828</i></div>
            </div>
          </div>
        </div>

        <div class="moment rise">
          <div class="tagrow"><span class="num">#2</span><span class="status-chip">When real organizers arrived</span></div>
          <h3>The organizers wanted calm, not cool</h3>
          <div class="prose"><p>We first designed the organizer side like the attendee side: modern and icon-heavy. The organizers who signed up were often over 60 and new to digital tools.</p></div>
          <div class="quote"><p>"I just need sales data. Where do I settle payments?"</p><cite>An organizer, on the first dashboard</cite></div>
          <div class="prose"><p>So we rebuilt it for clarity: <strong>text labels instead of icons, bigger text, simple tabs and one obvious "Create Event" button.</strong></p></div>
          <div class="compare rise" style="--ar: 16 / 9.4">
            <img src="/images/eventgem-dash-before.webp" alt="Before: Eventful dashboard full of empty widgets, icons and graphics, with no clear starting point" width="1440" height="810" loading="lazy" />
            <img class="after" src="/images/eventgem-dash-after.webp" alt="After: EventGem events page with text labels and one clear Create Event button" width="1442" height="964" loading="lazy" />
            <span class="tag b">Before</span><span class="tag a">After</span>
            <span class="divider"></span>
            <input type="range" min="0" max="100" value="50" aria-label="Drag to compare the old and new organizer dashboard" />
            <span class="knob" aria-hidden="true">⇆</span>
          </div>
          <span class="compare-note hand">drag me ⇆</span>
          <figure class="fig rise">
            <div class="frame"><img src="/images/eventgem-create-event.webp" alt="EventGem create event flow with a step list on the left and the Event Details form" width="1440" height="960" loading="lazy" /></div>
            <figcaption>Hit "Create Event" and the steps are spelled out in plain words, from details to preview.</figcaption>
          </figure>
        </div>

        <div class="moment rise">
          <div class="tagrow"><span class="num">#3</span><span class="status-chip">After launch</span></div>
          <h3>A huge crowd showed up, so the scanner slimmed down</h3>
          <div class="prose">
            <p>EventGem got picked for a fair with a crowd way bigger than we'd designed for. The first scanner loaded the full attendee list and live updates on every device, and under that load it gave up. We asked one design question: <strong>does a door manager need any of this mid-rush?</strong></p>
            <p>Nope. Their job is scan, yes or no, next person. So we cut the screen down to just a scanner, and removing the extra data fixed the crash too.</p>
          </div>
          <div class="compare tall rise" style="--ar: 430 / 900">
            <img src="/images/eventgem-scan-before.webp" alt="Before: scanner screen with event details, attendee data and live updates" width="900" height="2014" loading="lazy" />
            <img class="after" src="/images/eventgem-scan-after.webp" alt="After: a scanner that shows one clear success result and a Scan Next button" width="860" height="1774" loading="lazy" />
            <span class="tag b">Before</span><span class="tag a">After</span>
            <span class="divider"></span>
            <input type="range" min="0" max="100" value="50" aria-label="Drag to compare the old and new door scanner" />
            <span class="knob" aria-hidden="true">⇆</span>
          </div>
          <p class="disclaimer">I wasn't on site, I was in India. What happened at the gate came from our clients and team lead.</p>
        </div>
      </div>
    </section>

    <section class="cs-sec">
      <div class="wrap">
        <span class="step mono">07 · Outcome</span>
        <h2 class="reveal">It went live <em>while we were still building it</em></h2>
        <ul class="chain">
          <li>Launched mid-project</li><li class="arrow" aria-hidden="true">→</li><li>Real events ran</li><li class="arrow" aria-hidden="true">→</li><li>Real feedback</li><li class="arrow" aria-hidden="true">→</li><li class="end">Better product</li>
        </ul>
        <div class="wins">
          <div class="rise"><b>Many events hosted</b><span>Up and running for Indian communities overseas</span></div>
          <div class="rise"><b>Happy organizers</b><span>With both the platform and the service</span></div>
          <div class="rise"><b>Smooth door check-ins</b><span>No complaints from door managers since the rebuild</span></div>
        </div>
        <p class="disclaimer">What I'd measure next: scan time and error rate at the gate.</p>
      </div>
    </section>

    <section class="cs-sec">
      <div class="wrap">
        <span class="step mono">08 · Takeaways</span>
        <h2 class="reveal">Three things I carry <em>into every project</em></h2>
        <div class="principles" style="grid-template-columns: repeat(auto-fit, minmax(220px, 1fr))">
          <article class="pr rise"><span class="num mono">From the rebrand</span><h3>Change is part of the job</h3><span class="from">panic</span><span class="to hand">put a process around it</span></article>
          <article class="pr rise"><span class="num mono">From the organizers</span><h3>A persona is a starting point</h3><span class="from">trust the first guess</span><span class="to hand">real users get the final say</span></article>
          <article class="pr rise"><span class="num mono">From the crowd</span><h3>Design for the moment</h3><span class="from">show everything</span><span class="to hand">mid-rush, less is more</span></article>
        </div>
        <NextProject current="eventgem" />
      </div>
    </section>
  </article>
</Base>
